# Everything here is sent to the build daemon before the first instruction
# runs, so this file is about what the image build genuinely needs: the Go
# source, the web source, and the two manifests. Nothing else.
#
# Two of these are correctness, not speed. Read the Dockerfile alongside it.

# The drive's own data: files, index.db, trash, thumbnails, certificates. It is
# bind-mounted at run time and has no business in a build context — on a real
# instance this is the largest directory on the machine, and shipping a copy of
# someone's private files into an image layer is the worst outcome in this file.
/data/

# Installed for the host. The web stage runs `npm ci` against the manifests and
# then copies web/ over the top, so a host node_modules would bury the
# freshly-installed one — and these are platform-specific binaries: the host is
# glibc, the build image is Alpine musl, and esbuild would refuse to run.
web/node_modules/
node_modules/

# Built by the web stage inside the image and copied into the Go stage from
# there. A host copy would be overwritten anyway; excluding it keeps a stale
# local build from ever being a question.
web/dist/

# Release artifacts from scripts/release.sh, and a local `go build` output.
/dist/
/drive

# History, tooling, and design records. None of it compiles.
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.claude/
.serena/
.impeccable/
openspec/

# Tests that never run inside the image. The Go ones have to stay: they sit in
# the same packages as the code and `go build` still parses the directory.
web/e2e/
